description: Treat phone, iPad, and desktop as first-class layouts — never patch later
alwaysApply: true
---

# Viewports

Every layout, component, and interaction must work on phone, iPad, and desktop in the same pass. Do not ship a desktop design and retrofit smaller screens.

- Design from a real phone width (~390px), an iPad portrait/landscape band (~768–1024px), and desktop (~1280px+) before considering the work done.
- iPad is its own layout, not “mobile but wider” and not a shrunk desktop.
- Touch is the default on phone and iPad: hit targets at least 44px, no hover-only actions, no hover-only content. Hover may enhance desktop; it must not be required.
- Respect safe areas (`env(safe-area-inset-*)`), notch, and home indicator. Prevent horizontal overflow.
- Prefer CSS (flex, grid, container queries, fluid type/spacing) over JS for layout. Use `pointer: coarse | fine` when hover vs tap should differ.
- Navigation, typography, spacing, and motion must feel native on each surface — not a scaled desktop page.
